From a38aa34eae6ce56a931ba1c386ebe0cdf2f23f14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Khadas Edge1 Android TV <edge1@localhost>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Copy frames above 1080p on two threads

Khadas Edge1 (RK3399), Android 14. With the decode beside the copy (patch
0004) and the frame on a display plane, card 28 played 4K at 30 fps with
the component thread at two thirds of a core: per frame 13-20 ms copying
12.4 MB into the output buffer, 1.5 ms mapping, 4-5 ms waiting for the
decoder. For 4K60 the copy alone is over budget on one core, while four of
the six cores sat mostly idle.

An NV12 frame above 1080p is now copied in bands of 64 rows (both planes)
that the threads take in turn, so a slower core takes fewer bands and no
split has to be guessed. The component thread is one of them; the helpers
are started per frame (pthread, tens of microseconds) and joined before the
buffer goes out, and one that cannot be started leaves its bands to the
rest. persist.vendor.edge1.hwdec_copy_threads, 1-4, default 2; 1080p and
below stay on one thread (4 ms). Checked on the host: identical output for
odd sizes and 1-4 threads, clean under ThreadSanitizer.
---
 C2FFMPEGVideoDecodeComponent.cpp | 75 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 C2FFMPEGVideoDecodeComponent.h   |  2 +
 2 files changed, 74 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

